BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:English Conversation Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T113000
UID:6a6385869943bdf31ea13ed9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Would you like to improve your English speaking skills in a r
 elaxing and supportive environment?  We offer conversation prompts to ge
 t you talking about topics you enjoy. This is a great way to improve your
  English speaking skills and make new friends.  Learners at all levels a
 re welcome. Please note this is\nnot\na formal English class - assessment
  and evaluation are\nnot\nprovided.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6385869943bdf31ea13ed9
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Advanced English Conversation Circles (Level 5 & up) with WoodGree
 n
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261018T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261018T153000
UID:6a501360fb418a280099d5be@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:If you are a newcomer to Canada and want to enhance your Engli
 sh communication skills\, this free program is for you! Please note\, this
  is an opportunity to practice your conversational skills—it is not a f
 ormal English class.\nThis program is in partnership with WoodGreen Commun
 ity Services.\nAfter registering online\, you will be contacted by WoodGre
 en staff to complete your registration.\nPlease note\, there will be a bre
 ak in August\, with the program resuming on September 13th. WoodGreen wil
 l contact new registrants at the beginning of September.\nInformation Col
 lection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the
  Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 
 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program
  registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library h
 andles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline
 @tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, Second floor program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a501360fb418a280099d5be
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Specialty Coffee: From Your First Brew to Barista for Newcomers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T150000
UID:6ab2e44a19094f0c693949d4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​Want to take your love of coffee beyond a cup of cappuccino
 ? Thinking about opening your own café or launching a coffee brand? Explo
 re real-world career paths in coffee - from café barista to roaster to co
 ffee entrepreneur. Find your entry point in this industry and learn about 
 what works\, what doesn’t\, and what to avoid.\nPresented by Hong Dai\, 
 owner of Another Land Coffee\, a specialty coffee shop located in North Yo
 rk\, with over 15 years of experience in the specialty coffee and hospital
 ity industry.\nThis program is part of TPL Small Business Month.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Room B
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab2e44a19094f0c693949d4
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
