BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newcomer Settlement Services
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T170000
UID:69c1d0efbfe6da1042250b04@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New to Canada? Need information on employment\, housing\, lang
 uage learning\, schools\, or other topics? A Settlement Worker can help. D
 rop in to meet our settlement worker every Tuesday afternoon from 2 pm-5 p
 m.\nVisit our branch or contact Ada Tao at 416-770-0312 or atao@cathcrossc
 ultural.org.\nIn partnership with Catholic Crosscultural Services.\nPlease
  bring your immigration documents (PR card) with you
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Front Entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c1d0efbfe6da1042250b04
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Building Your Personal and Business Brand for Newcomers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T193000
UID:6aa32bf64ea230006f339b04@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​This introductory workshop is designed to help newcomers in
  Canada identify and manage their personal brand in alignment with their p
 rofessional goals. It covers key business branding elements and offers act
 ionable steps to enhance brand presence. Through interactive activities\, 
 participants will apply their learnings to develop both personal and busin
 ess brands\, while exploring marketing strategies and campaign elements su
 ited to their new environment.
LOCATION:Highland Creek\, Program Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa32bf64ea230006f339b04
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Refugee Sponsorship Training Program (RSTP) Free Information Sessi
 on
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T200000
UID:6aabed5c6074830038279367@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you a newly arrived refugee to Canada who would like to br
 ing your immediate family here under the 'One-Year Window' program? Or\, a
 re you someone in Canada who wants to help bring refugee family or friends
  abroad to Canada under the 'Private Sponsorship of Refugees' program? In 
 collaboration with Toronto Public Library\, the Refugee Sponsorship Traini
 ng Program (RSTP) is offering you a free information session about how bot
 h programs work.\nRegistration is required.\nPlease register online via (c
 lick here:\nEventbrite\n)
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 401\, 4th Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aabed5c6074830038279367
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
