DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T203000
UID:6aa08a274995480655ee01e2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:NOTE\n: Tuesdays\nOctober 6th and 13th\nclasses will be held i
 n Room B1 in the basement. Library staff or security will need to scan for
  access to the basement.\nPressing the down button on the elevator will no
 t work without assistance. October 20th to December 8th will resume in the
  Discussion Room on the 3rd floor.\nCultureLink offers a 10 week session t
 o prepare for the Citizenship test. Attend every week to improve your skil
 ls.\n- Learn about the test's content and structure\n- Get support and tip
 s from our Volunteer Mentors\n- Practice with sample quizzes\nFunded by Im
 migration\, Refugees and Citizenship Canada in Partnership with Toronto Pu
 blic Library.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on
  this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Lib
 raries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only
  be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Que
 stions about how the library handles your information can be directed to A
 nswerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\
 , Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Basement\, Room B1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa08a274995480655ee01e2
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
